    "deployment_notes": "Download both checkpoints at the pinned revisions into ${MODEL_ROOT} first (about 193 GB). The server listens on every interface inside the container and has no API key: publish the port only on a trusted network, or add VLLM_API_KEY. The first start compiles kernels and takes several minutes; the ${CACHE_ROOT} mount keeps them for later starts. Uses about 0.95 of each card's memory.",
    "differences_from_recipe": "The recipe's serve.sh binds 127.0.0.1 on the host; inside the container the server binds 0.0.0.0. Paths are /opt/venv and /models/...; CUDA_HOME is the image's /usr/local/cuda (13.3.1, the toolkit version the recipe was validated with). Everything else is serve.sh's default argv and environment for TP=4 with the DFlash drafter.",
    "draft": {
      "method": "dflash",
      "num_speculative_tokens": 3,
      "precision": "BF16",
      "repository": "incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2",
      "revision": "bf582e4eacc1810f76656d1811693ff6c6737d2a"
    },
    "hardware_configuration": "Four CMP 170HX cards, each exposing 64 GB on a PCIe Gen2 x16 link (modified cards; stock cards expose 8 GB on x4). Tensor parallel 4 assumes x16 links; on x4 links it is bus-bound and far slower than the numbers attached here. Power limit 180 W per card, set by the operator; the launch changes no power, clock or fan setting.",
    "peer_to_peer": "Off in this launch (VLLM_ALLOW_PCIE_P2P_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE=0): tensor-parallel all-reduces go through a host shared-memory path. The recipe's optional mode, for systems where the driver grants PCIe peer access, sets VLLM_ALLOW_PCIE_P2P_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE=1 and PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:False.",
    "quality": {
      "conditions": "Release 1.3.0 defaults, peer-to-peer off, measured on the native install (not in the container). HumanEval allows 4,096 tokens per reply and scores the last complete code block.",
